{"title":"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(faster_and_more_concise)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (faster and more concise)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/c/a8cd34b7d7cd56ef906a47f0ba95548092641d49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2^n3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> are non-negative integers, for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/808e3fb319c128b201239069e7725c4f26b16769.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^6$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is not a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748c3be4ba11c6529f93d586163d44a4f9be40de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^a$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/c/a8cd34b7d7cd56ef906a47f0ba95548092641d49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2^n3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/808e3fb319c128b201239069e7725c4f26b16769.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^6$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748c3be4ba11c6529f93d586163d44a4f9be40de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^a$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" />, and find all pairs of non-negative integers (n,m) for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcbff862353c43df245716ba098882452dfb7dfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2^n3^m)^{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" /> is not a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/e/51eb7b7dc8b7fd28ec836382033ea43ccd9b2d55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{2^n3^m}$\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying both expressions:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b31fb8141e89be39cf99d091339c9d357a4baf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{6n} \\cdot 3^{6m}$\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" /> is not a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/c/78cbe5d5dbc8bf856a082b7b388b0cc87c07e2e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n3^m} \\cdot 3^{2^n3^m}$\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Comparing both exponents (noting that there must be either extra powers of 2 or extra powers of 3 in the left expression):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/0/1f04a386d4b540ded0edd31880f08f227ad0c14d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6n &gt; 2^n3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" />  OR  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/3/a23b49403202c6301c0914cc973288d2b999f129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6m &gt; 2^n3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\nUsing the first inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/0/1f04a386d4b540ded0edd31880f08f227ad0c14d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6n &gt; 2^n3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" /> and going case by case starting with n <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/134004c561e4c0cca193dbf5122e5ca963dd5b7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\in$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> {0, 1, 2, 3...}:\n</p><p>n=0:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb336f5d19ee1e0790bbec234b38f5e090ab0b3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&gt;1 \\cdot 3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" /> which has no solution for non-negative integers m \n</p><p>n=1:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/979c912407660622659043593179341c21e6bc36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 &gt; 2 \\cdot 3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" /> which is true for m=0 but fails for higher integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/f/21fac631e1d5a04eb85567050e20aa72bfaa9550.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow (1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>n=2:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3bafae23544a839effc12fbaa5706bcf77d3e5a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 &gt; 4 \\cdot 3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" /> which is true for m=0 but fails for higher integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcb600fe5ba853ce65a7ccce14d4094217bcdf5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow (2,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>n=3:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/8/8283ae8b1be4041c8a4b289a410f9717e5325fd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 &gt; 8 \\cdot 3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" /> which is true for m=0 but fails for higher integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e79e3b54af3f1fcdec77d072b2df237d241e565b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow (3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>n=4:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/9/6e9ffbbd0efecdc7569e00235e66deea6236ba6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 &gt; 16 \\cdot 3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"94\" height=\"13\" /> which is true for m=0 but fails for higher integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4bae009f85b72c50e6b4d11b01e58edb7fc7cfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow (4,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>n=5:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58f579f995a55aa79365b75b70d48a5a600d3dd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 &gt; 32 \\cdot 3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"94\" height=\"13\" /> which has no solution for non-negative integers m \n</p><p>There are no more solutions for higher <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, as polynomials like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d621409978709c8c25a6a8e42a7d4fd78bb57ac1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> grow slower than exponentials like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Using the second inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/3/a23b49403202c6301c0914cc973288d2b999f129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6m &gt; 2^n3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> and going case by case starting with m <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/134004c561e4c0cca193dbf5122e5ca963dd5b7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\in$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> {0, 1, 2, 3...}:\n</p><p>m=0:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfd05d8e8fea8c675912eac0326701263257c2d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&gt;2^n \\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" /> which has no solution for non-negative integers n \n</p><p>m=1:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d65f00cec3e4200519a130d9965d8edd156071c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6&gt;2^n \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> which is true for n=0 but fails for higher integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65b965ecdba0057b4aa2684f5d930e2f55024917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow (0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>m=2:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bbc0302f3b3615ba004b6b689340cd0dc1f7d5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12&gt;2^n \\cdot 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> which is true for n=0 but fails for higher integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41d69a9a61e2b5bd6847bb33a327012d71d89662.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow (0,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>m=3:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/3/9a301ed6d056b39e9fbfe14bbdec92b66a6423f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18&gt;2^n \\cdot 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> which has no solution for non-negative integers n \n</p><p>There are no more solutions for higher <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, as polynomials like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/a/15a717b58292e0c0ab98767c4fb3ebc3a1a8ee10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6m$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> grow slower than exponentials like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/d/4edea0898ecea36c012496c1ca57ba3584bf3670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^m$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThus there are six numbers corresponding to (1,0), (2,0), (3,0), (4,0), (0,1), and (0,2).  \nPlugging them back into the original expression, these numbers are 2, 4, 8, 16, 3, and 9, respectively.  Their sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/6718ee32712ee7ec2e541566f35c94464f31dfa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\framebox{042}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28faster_and_more_concise.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(faster_and_more_concise)\">Solution 2 (faster and more concise)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (faster and more concise)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the condition is equivalent to saying\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d747b3a29cd71d59d0aaaf219a7815738731b4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[v_2(a^6) \\geq v_2(6^a) \\implies 6n \\geq a\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4c77fff40f1b6b4a37b27e70178404f2f1d09ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[v_3(a^6) \\geq v_3(6^a) \\implies 6m \\geq a.\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Notice that we cannot have both expressions to be equality state, as that would result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/841a0cecc848be006d2114c26d8e8e9f0e09b20d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^6 = 6^a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" /> Testing, we see the possible pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6d6f10a89b538ad0258486aee2c78a801c7f3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n, m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3daf1ac276859f5508c715fe808f356b03b5e8ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 0), (2, 0), (3, 0), (4, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"286\" height=\"18\" />  Since the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> grows much faster than the left-hand side of the above inequalities, these are all possible solutions.  Adding, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/6718ee32712ee7ec2e541566f35c94464f31dfa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\framebox{042}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"22\" />. \n</p><p>~Solution by Williamgolly\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II\" title=\"2002 AIME II\">2002 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2002\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195659\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 318/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8431/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.647      1 -total\n 58.16%    7.356      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.44%    4.988      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3124:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017195659 and revision id 235652. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}